{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"affordance affordance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","fileName":"Affordance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Affordance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]] [[Player Experience Layers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Player Experience Layers","Conceptual Model","3D User Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"affordance affordance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","fileName":"Affordance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Affordance","heading":"Affordance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An affordance is a property that helps a user understand or perform an action. Affordances help the user's [[Conceptual Model]] match the intended design.\n\nFour useful categories are:\n\n- Cognitive affordances help decide what action to take.\n- Physical affordances help carry out the action.\n- Functional affordances help accomplish a higher-level task.\n- Sensory affordances help perceive state or recognize an outcome.\n\nFor example, a visible virtual eraser can suggest deletion, being within reach can make selection physically possible, its behavior supplies deletion functionality, and highlighting on contact can make the interaction perceptible. A [[3D User Interface]] must often consider all four categories together.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Player Experience Layers","Conceptual Model","3D User Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"affordance affordance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Affordance.md","fileName":"Affordance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Affordance","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[gamesdesignandplay.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Player Experience Layers","Conceptual Model","3D User Interface","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}